    ("faillock deny", "`faillock` tallies auth failures (deny after N); unlock with `--user x --reset` — brute-force defense with self-lockout risk."),
    ("chage password aging", "`chage -M 90 user` enforces rotation; `-l` audits expiry before lockouts surprise on-call rotations."),
    ("lastlog wtmp", "`lastlog` shows every user's latest login (stale accounts stand out); `last -x` adds shutdown/runlevel history."),
    ("sosreport support", "`sosreport` bundles logs/configs for vendor tickets; `--clean` obfuscates IPs/hostnames before uploading."),
    ("tuned profiles", "`tuned-adm profile latency-performance|virtual-guest` applies workload presets (scheduler, disk, network knobs) in one switch."),
    ("irqbalance numa", "`irqbalance` spreads device interrupts across CPUs/NUMA nodes; database/network boxes verify placement with `numastat`."),
    ("kdump crash kernel", "`kdump` boots a capture kernel on panic for vmcore analysis; test with `echo c > /proc/sysrq-trigger` in maintenance windows only."),
    ("dnf yum install", "`dnf install pkg` (RHEL/Fedora, replaces yum); `dnf update` upgrades, `dnf history undo` rolls back transactions — repo-based with rollback, `rpm -qf` traces file owners."),
    ("pacman arch update", "`pacman -Syu` full upgrades (Arch: never partial `-Sy` without `-u`!); `pacman -S pkg` installs, `-Rns` removes with deps; AUR helpers (`yay`) build user repos — rolling release kept whole, never half-updated."),
    ("snap flatpak universal", "`snap install`/`flatpak install flathub` bundle deps (sandboxed, big); classic confinement (`--classic`) escapes for IDEs — distro packages preferred (native, small), universals for missing/proprietary apps."),
    ("systemctl enable start", "`systemctl enable --now app` enables+starts in one; `status` shows state+recent logs; `is-active/is-enabled` script halves separately — enable persists boot, start runs now, both verified."),
    ("journalctl follow since", "`journalctl -u app -f` tails one service; `--since '1h ago'` + `-p err` slices incidents; `-o json-pretty` structures for pipelines — centralized logs queried, never grepped raw across hosts."),
    ("dmesg errors boot", "`dmesg -T -l err,warn` kernel trouble (disks, OOM, drivers) with human time; `journalctl -k -b -1` previous boot — hardware truth before application theories, boot failures read here first."),
    ("lsblk fdisk mkfs", "`lsblk -f` maps disks/filesystems/mounts; `fdisk /dev/sdb` partitions (g/GPT!); `mkfs.ext4 -L data` formats; `blkid` UUIDs for fstab — partition→format→UUID→fstab→mount, in that order, verified each step."),
    ("mount fstab umount", "`UUID=xxx /data ext4 defaults,nofail 0 2` mounts by UUID (device names lie!); `nofail` boots past missing disks; `umount -l` lazy-detaches busy mounts (find culprits with `lsof +D`) — fstab reviewed (`findmnt --verify`) before reboots."),
    ("swapon zram swap", "`swapon -s` lists; `fallocate -l 2G /swap && chmod 600 && mkswap && swapon` file swap; zram (`zram-generator`) compressed RAM swap for desktops — swap sized to hibernation needs (RAM+), swappiness tuned per workload."),
    ("sysctl net tune", "`sysctl -w net.ipv4.ip_forward=1` live; persist in `/etc/sysctl.d/*.conf` (reboot wipes runtime-only!); `net.core.somaxconn` listen queues, `vm.swappiness` reclaim bias — runtime tweaks tested, files persist, both or neither."),
    ("ufw allow order", "`ufw allow 22/tcp` then `ufw enable` (SSH FIRST or lockout!); `ufw status numbered` + `delete N` manages; `default deny incoming` posture — firewall before exposure, test from outside (nmap), never assume."),
    ("firewalld zones services", "`firewall-cmd --permanent --add-service=https --zone=public` then `--reload`; zones (public/dmz/trusted) per interface; `--add-rich-rule` fine-grained — permanent+reload pattern (runtime-only vanishes on reload!)."),
    ("iptables nftables input", "`iptables -A INPUT -m conntrack --ctstate ESTABLISHED,RELATED -j ACCEPT` + service rules + `DROP` default (`iptables-save` persists!); nftables (`nft add rule ...`) atomic whole-ruleset loads — default-drop with established fast-pathed, rules versioned in git."),
    ("fail2ban jail status", "`fail2ban-client status sshd` shows bans; jails (`sshd`, `nginx-limit-req`) parse logs → iptables (bantime/findtime/maxretry tuned); `unbanip` rescues — brute force absorbed automatically, self-lockouts via whitelist (`ignoreip`)."),
    ("selinux enforcing diagnose", "`getenforce`/`setenforce 1` modes (enforcing/permissive/disabled); denials in AVC logs → `audit2why` explains → `semanage` fixes (never `setenforce 0` permanently!) — MAC denials diagnosed (contexts!), not disabled."),
    ("apparmor enforce complain", "`aa-status` shows enforce/complain modes; `aa-enforce/aa-complain` switch; `aa-genprof` learns from behavior — complain-then-enforce workflow (clean week before enforcing), profiles per application."),
    ("ssh keygen ed25519", "`ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C 'me@host'` modern keys (no passphrase-less privates on disk unencrypted!); `ssh-copy-id user@h` installs; `~/.ssh/config` aliases (`Host x HostName ...`) — keys replace passwords, config replaces memorized flags."),
    ("sshd config harden", "`PasswordAuthentication no` + `PubkeyAuthentication yes` + `PermitRootLogin prohibit-password` + `MaxAuthTries 3` + nonstandard `Port` (obscurity layer, not security); `sshd -T` validates before restart (lockout-proof!) — hardened, tested, then exposed."),
    ("ssh tunnel local remote", "`ssh -N -L 8080:localhost:80 h` local-forward (remote service locally); `-R 9000:localhost:3000 h` reverse (local service remotely); `-D 1080` SOCKS proxy — `-N` no shell, `-f` backgrounds, autossh resurrects."),
    ("scp rsync delete exclude", "`scp -r dir/ h:/srv/` simple copies; `rsync -avz --delete --exclude='.git/' src/ dst/` mirrors (trailing slash decides content-vs-dir! `--dry-run` first) — rsync for repeats (delta!), scp for one-offs, delete flags triple-checked."),
    ("cron format list", "`30 2 * * * /opt/b.sh >>/var/log/b.log 2>&1` (min hour dom mon dow); `crontab -l` lists, `-e` edits, `-r` REMOVES ALL (danger!); cron env minimal (absolute paths, explicit SHELL/PATH) — schedules logged (output anywhere but mail spool)."),
    ("anacron vs cron", "anacron (`/etc/anacrontab`: `1 15 job /opt/d.sh`) runs daily-ish even powered-off at 2am (laptops!); cron exact-time (servers!) — laptops anacron, servers cron, systemd timers for logging/dependencies."),
    ("systemd timer pair", "`.timer` (`OnCalendar=daily`, `Persistent=true` catch-up) + matching `.service` replaces cron with journal logging + dependencies + jitter (`RandomizedDelaySec`); `list-timers` audits all — timers where observability matters, cron where simplicity wins."),
    ("logrotate compress rotate", "`/var/log/app/*.log { daily rotate 14 compress delaycompress missingok }` bounds logs; `postrotate` signals daemons (reopen FDs!); `logrotate -d` debugs — rotation configured before disks fill (not after the 3am page)."),
    ("useradd usermod userdel", "`useradd -m -s /bin/bash -G sudo,dev app` provisions (home+shell+groups); `usermod -aG` appends (without -a REPLACES!); `userdel -r` removes home — `-a` flag memorized (bare usermod destroys memberships)."),
    ("passwd chage lock", "`passwd user` sets; `passwd -l` locks (keeps files/cron for forensics!); `chage -M 90 -W 7` rotation+warning; `chage -l` audits — lock (not delete) leavers first, rotation enforced not requested."),
    ("sudo visudo nopasswd", "`visudo` edits with syntax check (broken sudoers = no admins!); `user ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl restart app` scoped grants; `sudo -l` audits own rights — scoped commands (never ALL), validated syntax always."),
    ("last who w audit", "`last` wtmp logins/reboots/crashes (audit intrusions!); `who/w` current sessions; `lastlog` per-user latest (stale accounts stand out) — login history reviewed (weekly cron + alerts on unknown)."),
    ("uptime load cores", "`uptime` load 1/5/15min ÷ core count (`nproc`): 1.0/core = saturated; `w` adds who/what — loads contextualized per host (4.0 idle on 16 cores, dead on 2)."),
    ("free available buffers", "`free -h`: `available` (not `free`!) is real headroom (cache reclaimable); `free+buff/cache` mental math obsolete — available watched (alerts), free ignored (always near-zero on healthy Linux)."),
    ("vmstat si so wa", "`vmstat 1`: `si/so` swap in/out (any sustained = death), `wa` I/O wait, `us/sy/id` CPU split, `r/b` run/block queues — one line diagnoses CPU vs memory vs disk in 5 seconds flat."),
    ("iostat await util", "`iostat -x 1`: `%util` ~100 = saturated disk, `await` latency, `avgqu-sz` depth; per-device (`sda` vs `nvme0n1`) isolates culprits — disk-bound proven (await/util), not guessed (slow app?)."),
    ("sar history install", "`sar -u -r -d -n DEV 1 3` live CPU/mem/disk/net; `-f /var/log/sa/saDD` replays yesterday (sysstat installed+enabled first or history never existed!) — todays incident vs yesterdays baseline, same tool."),
    ("mpstat pidstat threads", "`mpstat -P ALL 1` per-CPU (one hot core = single-threaded bottleneck!); `pidstat -t 1` per-thread (`-u/-r/-d` CPU/mem/IO) — per-CPU/thread views find serialization the totals hide."),
    ("perf top symbols", "`perf top` live hot functions (kernel+user symbols!); `perf record -g` + `perf report` call graphs; `perf stat -e cache-misses` hardware counters — profile first (symbols!), optimize second (widest frame)."),
    ("htop setup tree", "`htop` (F2 setup: meters/columns, F5 tree, F9 kill, `/` filter, `u` per-user); `t` tree shows parentage; `H` threads — interactive triage (sorting by CPU/MEM/TIME), `atop` for history (netatop kernel module for per-process net)."),
    ("iotop iftop nethogs", "`iotop -o` disk I/O by process (who eats the disk!); `iftop -i eth0` per-connection traffic; `nethogs` per-process net — I/O attribution per process (not per disk), run as root for full visibility."),
    ("ss state filter", "`ss -t state established '( dport = :443 )'` filters precisely; `-s` summarizes; `-p` owns processes; `-tlnp` listening staple — ss scripts everything netstat did (deprecated!), filters replace grep pipelines."),
    ("lsof deleted unmount", "`lsof | grep deleted` finds unlinked-but-open files (disk full with free space! — restart holders or `: > file`); `lsof +D /data` pre-unmount audit — deleted-open is the classic phantom-full-disk."),
    ("ps forest select", "`ps auxf` forest (parentage!); `ps -eo pid,ppid,%cpu,%mem,cmd --sort=-%cpu` ranks; `o=` custom columns; `STAT` flags (D uninterruptible sleep = disk!) — forest for relationships, custom columns for scripts."),
    ("timeout kill watchdog", "`timeout 30 cmd` (exit 124 on kill!); `-s KILL` escalates; `--preserve-status` forwards real codes; `timeout 10 bash -c '</dev/tcp/h/80'` probes — hangs bounded everywhere (cron/network/scripts), 124 handled distinctly."),
    ("watch diff monitor", "`watch -n2 -d 'ss -tlnp'` highlights changes live (deploys/queues!); `-d=cumulative` accumulates; `-x` exact exec — poor-man's dashboards, `while sleep` loops retired."),
    ("hardware info oneline", "`lscpu` (arch/flags/cores), `lsmem` (zones), `lsblk -f` (disks/mounts), `lspci -k` (drivers!), `lsusb`, `dmidecode -t system` (serial!), `sensors` (temps!) — one command per subsystem (no reboot diagnostics blind)."),
    ("boot systemd analyze", "`systemd-analyze blame` (slowest units!) + `critical-chain` (path!); `journalctl -b -1 -p err` last boot errors; `systemctl --failed` broken units — boot slowness blamed per unit (mask/disable culprits), failures listed not guessed."),
    ("nice ionice renice", "`nice -n 10 longjob` deprioritizes CPU; `renice` adjusts live; `ionice -c3` idles disk hogs (best-effort class 2 default!) — noisy neighbors tamed (batch deprioritized, interactive protected), kills last resort."),
    ("taskset numactl pin", "`taskset -c 0-3 app` pins CPUs (cache warmth, license cores!); `numactl --cpunodebind=0 --membind=0` NUMA-localizes (remote memory = slow!) — pinning measured (cross-NUMA penalties proven with `numastat`), not superstition."),
    ("ip addr route link", "`ip -br a` compact addresses; `ip r` default routes; `ip link set dev up/mtu` controls; `ip neigh` ARP table (`FAILED` = L2 problem!) — `ip` replaces ifconfig/route/arp (deprecated!), one tool, scriptable output."),
    ("traceroute mtr hops", "`traceroute` per-hop latency (ICMP filtered lies! use `-T -p 443` TCP mode); `mtr --report` loss% per hop (loss at hop N + clean beyond = that hop deprioritizes ICMP, not broken!) — hop analysis reads loss PATTERNS, not single numbers."),
    ("dig short trace", "`dig +short A x.my` answers only (scripts!); `dig @8.8.8.8` pins resolver; `+trace` walks delegation (finds WHO lies); `+dnssec` validates — resolver pinned when debugging (systemd-resolved/stub games exposed)."),
    ("rsync daemon backup", "`rsync -avz --delete --link-dest=/b/latest /data/ /b/$(date +%F)/` hard-link snapshots (full views, incremental space!); daemon mode (`rsync://`) for pull backups — snapshot rotation scripted (7 daily/4 weekly), restores tested."),
    ("restore borg restic test", "Borg (`borg extract repo::date`) / restic (`restic restore latest --target /tmp/r`) restores rehearsed quarterly to staging + app smoke tests — restores tested (checksums insufficient!), RTO measured (assumptions die here)."),
    ("man sections read", "`man 1 printf` (user command) vs `man 3 printf` (C function) — sections disambiguate same names (1 commands, 5 formats, 8 admin); NAME/SYNOPSIS/DESCRIPTION/OPTIONS/EXAMPLES structure skimmed (options first, examples last) — manuals read strategically, not top-to-bottom."),
    ("man help pager", "`cmd --help` (fast, alphabetical flags) before `man cmd` (deep: description + examples); `man` opens pager (`/search`, `n` next, `q` quit, `h` help) — help for flags (seconds), man for concepts (minutes), chosen per urgency (exams: --help first!)."),
    ("apropos mandb search", "`apropos -s 1,8 director` finds commands by description (generic stems match more: 'director' hits directories+directors!); `sudo mandb` builds the index (fresh VMs lack it!) — forgotten names found via purpose, `man -k` equivalent remembered."),
    ("tab completion double", "`systemctl list-dep<TAB><TAB>` lists options (double-TAB when ambiguous); path completion (`ls /u<TAB>` → `/usr/`) explores without listing; long names typed minimally (`wor<TAB>` → `wordpress_archive.tgz`) — completion saves hours monthly, bash-completion package enables per-command intelligence."),
    ("bash completion custom", "`complete -F _svc systemctl`-style functions fill `COMPREPLY` from context (services/hosts/branches); `complete -p` inspects, `complete -r` removes — custom completions for internal CLIs (flags/hosts), debugged with `set -x` inside functions."),
    ("info gnu pages", "`info coreutils 'ls invocation'` navigates GNU manuals (nodes/menus, deeper than man for coreutils!); `pinfo` colors; `/usr/share/doc/*/README*` package notes — info for GNU depth, man for breadth, doc dirs for package specifics."),
    ("whatis which type", "`whatis ls` one-line descriptions (needs mandb!); `which cmd` PATH-locates (misses aliases/functions!); `type -a cmd` reveals all layers (alias→function→builtin→file); `command -v` scripts safely — four tools, four truths (scripts use type/command, humans use which/whatis)."),
    ("help builtin command", "`help cd` documents shell builtins (man has no builtin pages!); `help -s` syntax-only; `enable -n echo` disables builtins (testing external behavior) — builtins helped via help, binaries via man, confused never."),
    ("kernel oops decode", "Oops (register dump + Call Trace!) decoded with `scripts/decode_stacktrace.sh` + `addr2line -e vmlinux` (debug symbols!); `dmesg -T` timestamps, `journalctl -k` persists — first oops captured complete (serial/netconsole if disk suspect), decoded with symbols, reported via `admin-guide/reporting-issues`."),
    ("sysrq magic keys", "`Alt+SysRq R-E-I-S-U-B` (unRaw, tErminate, kIll, Sync, Unmount, reBoot) revives wedged boxes safely; `echo c > /proc/sysrq-trigger` crash-tests kdump (maintenance ONLY!); `kernel.sysrq` sysctl gates (`1` all, `0` off) — magic keys before power buttons, always."),
    ("livepatch no reboot", "Livepatch (`kpatch`/`klp`) applies CVE fixes without reboots (`cat /sys/kernel/livepatch/*/enabled` verifies); not for major versions (reboots still scheduled!) — uptime preserved for patches, maintenance windows for upgrades (honest about limits)."),
    ("kernel cmdline params", "`GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX=\"...\"` + `update-grub` persists boot params (`mitigations=`, `cgroup_no_v1=`, `crashkernel=`); `/proc/cmdline` verifies live — boot params versioned (git!), tested one-shot via GRUB edit (recovery if wrong)."),
    ("transparent hugepages", "`/sys/kernel/mm/transparent_hugepage/enabled` (`always/madvise/never`): databases want `madvise`/`never` (latency spikes from khugepaged!), HPC wants `always` — THP tuned per workload (DB vendors document `never`, measured per host)."),
    ("ksm dedup memory", "KSM (`/sys/kernel/mm/ksm/run=1`, `ksmtuned`) dedupes identical pages (VMs/containers share liberally!); `pages_sharing` measures savings — KSM for homogeneous fleets (VDI/CI), CPU cost metered (`ksmd` cycles)."),
    ("zswap zram writeback", "zswap (compressed RAM cache before disk swap, `zswap.enabled=1`) + zram writeback devices (`echo lz4 > /sys/block/zram0/comp_algorithm`) — compressed swap tiers beat disk swap 10x latency; desktops/laptops default, servers measured."),
    ("lockdown integrity mode", "Lockdown (`integrity`/`confidentiality`, `cat /sys/kernel/security/lockdown`) blocks raw mem/kexec unsigned modules; Secure Boot chain (shim→MOK→kernel, `mokutil --sb-state` verifies) — lockdown for compliance images (debug needs confinement exemptions, planned)."),
    ("crashkernel kdump size", "`crashkernel=512M` reserves capture memory (sized to RAM! `crashkernel=auto` distros); `kdumpctl status` + `kdumpctl estimate` verify — reservation proven (`kdumpctl` active), test crash in maintenance (echo c), vmcore analyzed (crash/gdb)."),
    ("nmi watchdog lockup", "`nmi_watchdog=1` + `watchdog_thresh` (softlockup panics: `softlockup_panic=1`) catch wedged CPUs (all-cores-busy-forever = real hang!); `hung_task_timeout_secs` flags D-state piles — watchdogs enabled (false positives investigated, never blanket-disabled)."),
    ("earlyoom nohang oomd", "earlyoom (`-m 10 -s 60`: kill at 10% free!) / nohang (PSI-aware, kinder) / systemd-oomd (cgroup pressure kills) beat kernel OOM lottery for desktops (browser tab reaped vs session death!) — userspace OOM tuned (kill lists!), kernel OOM last resort."),
    ("fstrim timer ssd", "`fstrim -Av` discards freed blocks (SSD GC!); `fstrim.timer` weekly (not continuous discard `discard` mount — latency!); `lsblk -D` verifies support — TRIM scheduled (weekly timer), discard mount avoided (latency spikes)."),
    ("unattended upgrades auto", "`unattended-upgrades` (`Unattended-Upgrade::Automatic-Reboot`) patches security automatically (reboot windows!); `needrestart` flags stale processes post-patch — auto-patch security (reboot policy explicit), manual majors (breaking changes reviewed)."),
    ("motd landscape info", "`/etc/motd` + `update-motd.d/*` scripts greet logins (updates pending! reboot required!); `landscape-sysinfo` rich stats — MOTD informs (patch status, reboots), never spams (admins ignore noisy logins)."),
    ("cockpit web console", "Cockpit (`systemctl enable --now cockpit.socket`, port 9090) web-manages (terminal! storage! services! updates!) with sudo bridging — GUI for occasional admins (audit logged!), CLI remains source of truth (automation)."),
    ("netdata install claim", "Netdata (`kickstart.sh`) per-second metrics (CPU/net/disk/apps!) with zero config; `netdata-claim.sh` clouds centralize — 1s granularity finds spikes minute-averages hide; retention sized (RAM!)."),
    ("glances htop atop pick", "htop (interactive triage: tree/filter/kill), atop (history daemon: `atop -r` replays!), glances (all-in-one: CPU/mem/net/disk/docker!) — htop now, atop yesterday, glances everything (API/export for dashboards)."),
    ("duf dust procs modern", "`duf` (disks with inodes+mounts, readable!), `dust` (visual tree usage), `procs` (process list with ports/tree!) — modern replacements learned once (aliases!), scripts keep POSIX originals (portability)."),
    ("bottom btm dashboard", "`btm` (Rust dashboard: CPU graphs per core, net sparklines, battery!) `--basic` script-safe; GPU temp widgets — dashboards for humans (trends!), parsers for scripts (JSON flags where offered)."),
    ("hyperfine benchmark cli", "`hyperfine --warmup 3 'grep x f' 'rg x f'` benchmarks (statistics, not vibes!); `--export-markdown` documents; `--prepare` resets state — claims measured (CI benches catch regressions), feelings retired."),
    ("entr watchexec rerun", "`ls *.c | entr -r make test` rebuilds on save; `watchexec -e rs -- ./run` filtered smarter — tight feedback loops (edit→test seconds), watchers scoped (broad globs hot-loop!)."),
    ("fzf history search", "`history | fzf` fuzzy-finds commands (`Ctrl-R` with fzf keybindings replaces it live!); `fd pattern | fzf` + `bat {}` previews — recall beats retyping (long one-liners found, not rewritten)."),
    ("starship zoxide direnv", "starship (`starship init bash`) informative prompt (git/lang/k8s, fast Rust!); `zoxide` (`z proj` frecency jumps); `direnv` (`.envrc` per-dir env, `direnv allow` trusts!) — shell ergonomics compounded daily (prompt/context/nav)."),
    ("asciinema record demo", "`asciinema rec demo.cast` records terminal sessions (timing-preserved!); `agg` GIFs; play/embedding shares — demos recorded (not screenshotted!), secrets redacted before publishing (env scrubbed)."),
    ("tldr pages examples", "`tldr tar` practical examples first (vs man exhaustive!); `tldr --update` refreshes; pages community-written — examples before theory (daily use), man for depth (edge cases)."),
    ("navi cheatsheets interactive", "`navi` fuzzy-searches cheatsheets (`--query docker`) then fills arguments interactively (prompts per `<arg>`!) — personal knowledge base executable (repo of cheats), team-shared via git."),
    ("bro pages concise", "`bro 'find files'` gives concise examples (shorter than man, honest than memory); community snippets — quick reminders (daily flags), man for contracts (exact semantics)."),
    ("ripgrep all pdf", "`rga pattern` searches PDFs/zips/DBs (adapters extract text!) — code+docs+archives one query; `.rgrc` configures adapters — full-corpus search (compliance sweeps!), binary-aware by default."),
    ("eza lsd modern ls", "`eza -la --git --icons` (git status inline! tree view!) / `lsd` alternatives; aliases replace ls interactively — modern listing daily (git integration!), scripts keep POSIX ls (everywhere present)."),
    ("man emulator sections", "Sections: 1 commands, 2 syscalls, 3 library, 5 formats, 8 admin (`man 5 passwd` vs `man 1 passwd` differ!); `man -k`/`apropos` searches descriptions — section-qualified lookups (ambiguity resolved), WHATIS database maintained (`mandb`)."),
    ("kernel admin guide map", "docs.kernel.org admin-guide: sysctl (`/proc/sys` live knobs!), boot params, oops reporting, locking, cgroups, namespaces, perf/tracing (ftrace/perf/eBPF!), livepatch, kdump — admin guide read per subsystem (tuned, not skimmed)."),
    ("ftrace function trace", "`trace-cmd record -p function_graph -l 'sys_*'` traces kernel functions (overhead measured!); `/sys/kernel/debug/tracing/` raw interface; function_graph shows call trees with timings — kernel-level profiling (latency root causes below syscalls)."),
    ("perf stat record report", "`perf stat -e cycles,cache-misses,cmd` hardware counters; `perf record -g` + `perf report` hot functions; `perf top` live — proof before optimizing (widest frame first!), flamegraphs (stackcollapse) visualize."),
    ("fault injection test", "`fail_function`/`failcmd` fault-injection (`/sys/kernel/debug/fail*`: slab/pagealloc/IO errors!) tests error paths (ENOMEM handling!); `should_fail` rates — resilience proven (chaos per-syscall), happy-path-only code exposed."),
    ("rhel alma rocky migrate", "RHEL (`subscription-manager register --auto-attach`!) vs Alma/Rocky (free rebuilds, `almalinux-deploy`/`migrate2rocky` convert in place!) vs Oracle (UEK default, RHCK optional!); EUS/ELS channels extend life (paid!) — subscriptions attached (repos enabled!), migrations tested (clones first!), UEK chosen deliberately (tested drivers!)."),
    ("suse manager ltss suma", "SUSE SCC registers (`SUSEConnect -r CODE`!); LTSS/ESPOS extend (paid channels!); SUMA manages (channels sync, staging, Salt states!); LTSS kernel live (TuxCare alternative!) — registered (repos!), staged (dev→prod channels!), patched scheduled (maintenance windows!)."),
    ("ubuntu pro esm landscape", "`pro attach TOKEN` enables ESM-apps/infra (10yr security!), CIS/FIPS/Livepatch (`pro enable livepatch/cis/fips`!); Landscape manages fleets (profiles!); `unattended-upgrades` from ESM — Pro attached (tokens vaulted!), Livepatch kernels (reboots deferred!), Landscape groups (staged rollouts!)."),
    ("tpm2 clevis tang luks", "`clevis luks bind -d /dev/sda2 tang '{\"url\":\"...\"}'` network-bound decryption (no passphrase at boot!); TPM2 PCRs measured-boot binding; `clevis luks unlock` initramfs hook — Tang highly-available (both servers! or locked out!), PCRs pinned (updates re-seal!), recovery keys escrowed (sealed envelope!)."),
    ("fido2 luks pkcs11 ssh", "`systemd-cryptenroll --fido2-device=auto` FIDO2 unlock (PIN + touch!); PKCS#11 smartcards (`p11-kit`, SSH `SecurityKeyProvider`!); `ssh-keygen -t ed25519-sk` resident keys — hardware auth (phishing-proof!), backup keys enrolled (lost token ≠ lost data!), PINs set (touch alone insufficient!)."),
    ("sssd freeipa realmd join", "`realm join --user=admin ipa.x.my` enrolls (SSSD configures!); `id user@x.my` verifies; sudo/HBAP rules central (`ipa hbacrule-add`!); `realm leave` cleans — enrolled (keytabs rotated!), HBAC gates sudo (per-host!), leave cleanly (stale principals hunted!)."),
    ("ansible vault dynamic inventory", "`ansible-vault encrypt_string` secrets (never plaintext vars!); dynamic inventory scripts/plugins (cloud-sourced hosts!); roles (`tasks/handlers/defaults/meta`!) reusable; `--check --diff` dry-runs — vaulted secrets (passwords vaulted, never logged!), inventories dynamic (CMDB truth!), roles versioned (galaxy pinned!)."),
    ("salt grains pillars masterless", "Grains target (`salt -G 'os:Ubuntu' test.ping`!), pillars secrete per-minion (`pillar.get`!), masterless (`salt-call --local`) edge; `salt-ssh` agentless — targeting tested (`test=True` first!), pillars encrypted (GPG renderer!), highstate idempotent (reruns safe!)."),
    ("puppet hiera enc server", "Hiera hierarchy (node→role→common eyaml-encrypted secrets!) + ENC classifies (Foreman!); `puppet agent -t` runs (noop `--noop` first!); PuppetDB facts queried — hierarchy ordered (specific wins!), secrets eyaml (keys managed!), ENC single source (sprawl dead!)."),
    ("maas power curtin hooks", "MAAS commissions (hardware inventory!) + power drivers (IPMI/Redfish! `power_address`!) + curtin `early/late-commands` customize; `maas $P machines deploy` scripts — power configured (tested cycles!), curtin hooks idempotent (re-runs safe!), commissioning data reviewed (firmware!)."),
    ("subiquity autoinstall schema", "Autoinstall YAML (`version: 1`, identity/storage/network/proxy!) validated (`subiquity --dry-run`!); `late-commands` (curtin in-target!); cloud-init layered after — schema validated (version!), late-commands chroot-aware (paths!), dry-run first (reinstalls cost hours!)."),
    ("kickstart pre post chroot", "`%pre` (outside chroot, network setup!) / `%post --chroot` (inside, packages/services!) / `%packages` explicit; Anaconda `inst.` boot options; Cobbler snippets templatize — %pre networks (static IPs!), %post configures (first-boot services!), logs preserved (`/root/anaconda-ks.cfg`!)."),
    ("cobbler distro profile", "`cobbler distro add --name=u24 --kernel=... --initrd=...` + `profile --distro --kickstart` + `system --profile --interface --mac` binds MAC→profile (PXE deterministic!); `cobbler sync` regenerates — snippets shared (common code!), systems pinned (MACs!), sync verified (TFTP!)."),
    ("foreman hostgroups proxies", "Host groups (OS/lifecycle/params inheritance!) + Smart Proxies (DHCP/DNS/TFTP/PuppetCA per subnet!) + parameters (host→group→global precedence!) — groups model fleets (params inherited!), proxies per site (latency!), parameters audited (overrides visible!)."),
    ("katello lifecycle composite", "Lifecycle Environments (Library→Dev→Stage→Prod promotion!) + Content Views (repos pinned!) + Composite (multi-repo atomic!) — promote tested (errata applied!), composites version (atomic sets!), capsules sync (bandwidth scheduled!)."),
    ("insights advisor remediate", "Insights (`insights-client --register`, advisor rules: security/perf/stability!) + remediations (Ansible playbooks auto-fix!) + compliance policies (OpenSCAP scans!) + vulnerability (CVE exposure!) — registered (inventory!), remediations reviewed (auto-apply scoped!), compliance scheduled (drift caught!)."),
    ("leapp inhibitors answerfile", "`leapp preupgrade` lists inhibitors (blocking!) + `/var/log/leapp/answerfile` (manual decisions pre-answered!) + `leapp upgrade` (reboot into upgrade env!); actors custom — inhibitors resolved (all green!), answerfile complete (prompts kill unattended!), snapshot first (rollback!)."),
    ("auditd rules ausearch", "`auditctl -w /etc/shadow -p wa -k identity` watches (immutable `-e 2` prod!); `ausearch -k identity -ts recent` queries; `aureport --summary` digests; `audisp-remote` forwards (central SIEM!) — rules versioned (git!), immutable prod (tamper-evident!), forwarded (local logs lie!)."),
    ("aide osquery fim wazuh", "AIDE (`aide --init`, DB baselined, `aide --check` daily!) file integrity; Osquery (`osqueryi`, packs scheduled, `file_events`!) live inventory; Wazuh syscheck (realtime! manager central!) — baselines built (clean images!), checks scheduled (drift alerted!), managers central (agents report!)."),
    ("tripwire lynis openscap", "Tripwire policy-tuned (`twadmin --create-polfile`, signed DBs!); Lynis (`lynis audit system`, CIS cats, hardening index!) advises; OpenSCAP (`oscap xccdf eval --profile xccdf...cis`) certifies — policies tuned (noise baselined!), audits scheduled (scores tracked!), remediate selected (risk-ordered!)."),
    ("vuls openvas nessus agents", "Vuls (agentless SSH scan, oval DBs!) / OpenVAS Greenbone (gvmd scans/tasks, credentials SMB/SSH!) / Nessus agents (offline `.nessus` imports!) — scans credentialed (depth!), scheduled (weekly!), remediated (SLAs per severity!), false positives tuned (exceptions documented!)."),
    ("falcon wazuh meshcentral edr", "Falcon sensor (kernel/userland, `falconctl stats`!) / Wazuh manager+agents (decoders/rules custom!) / MeshCentral (remote/file/routes, 2FA!) — sensors healthy (check-ins monitored!), rules tuned (noise baselined!), remote gated (MFA + audit!)."),
    ("rustdesk guacamole teleport", "RustDesk self-hosted relay (`hbbr`/`hbbs`, key pinned!) / Guacamole RDP/VNC/SSH gateways (recordings! TOTP!) / Teleport (`tsh ssh`, short-lived certs, session replay!) — relays owned (keys pinned!), recordings kept (forensics!), certs short-lived (no static creds!)."),
    ("squid forward icap bump", "Squid forward proxy (`http_port 3128`, ACLs `src/dst/port`, `http_access allow/deny` order!) + ICAP REQMOD/RESPMOD (ClamAV!) + SSL bump (`ssl_bump peek/splice`, CA deployed!) + delay pools (bandwidth classes!) — ACLs ordered (deny last!), bump disclosed (legal!), pools fair (abuse shaped!)."),
    ("tinyproxy privoxy transparent", "Tinyproxy (`Upstream`, `BasicAuth`, filter lists!) lightweight forward; Privoxy actions (`+block`, `+hide-referrer`, filters!) privacy; transparent (`iptables REDIRECT`, TPROXY marks!) — explicit configured (PAC/WPAD!), transparent declared (consent!), filters maintained (lists updated!)."),
    ("tproxy delay collapsed storeid", "TPROXY (`iptables -t mangle ... TPROXY`, policy routing marks!) preserves client IP (X-Forwarded lies avoided!); delay pools (class/aggregate!); collapsed_forwarding (thundering herd!); `store_id` program rewrites (query-stripped caching!) — marks routed (policy!), herds collapsed (origin shielded!), IDs normalized (hit rate!)."),
    ("icp peers snmp mgr templates", "Cache peers (`cache_peer sibling ... icp`) share (hierarchies!); SNMP (`snmp_port`, MIB counters `inSvcTime`!) monitors; `mgr:info` status (sweeper/storage/sec*!); error templates branded; external ACL (`session/concurrency/starttls`!) — peers measured (RTT!), SNMP polled (capacity!), templates branded (users informed!)."),
    ("kerberos ntlm ldap acl", "Squid helpers: Kerberos (`negotiate_kerberos_auth` keytabs!) / NTLM (`ntlm_sspi` children!) / LDAP (`basic_ldap_auth` groups!) — `auth_param` tuned (children concurrency!), groups authorize (not just authenticate!), fallback ordered (methods tried!)."),
    ("pac wpad dat proxy", "PAC (`FindProxyForURL`, `isInNet/dnsResolve/myIpAddress`!) served + `WPAD.dat` (DHCP 252/DNS `wpad`!) auto-discovers; `Alert()` debugs (parser!) — PAC tested (parser!), WPAD secured (attacker PAC = MITM! sign/HTTPS!), direct fallback (proxy down ≠ offline!)."),
    ("nginx stream upstream cache", "`stream { upstream db { server a:5432; } server { listen 5432; proxy_pass db; } }` TCP proxy (databases!); `upstream` keepalive/health (`max_fails`!); `proxy_cache` zones (keys/levels!); `limit_req/limit_conn` abuse; OCSP stapling (`ssl_stapling`!) — streams proxy TCP (TLS too!), caches zoned (keys designed!), limits protect (bursts shaped!)."),
    ("haproxy acl stick peers", "ACLs (`path_beg/host_hdr`!) route; `stick-table` + `stick on src` persist (peers sync `peers` section!); `balance leastconn/uri` algorithms; `http-request deny if` guards; DNS SRV resolvers discover — ACLs route (tested!), stickiness synced (peers!), algorithms matched (long-lived vs short!)."),
    ("envoy xds clusters eds", "Envoy xDS (LDS/RDS/CDS/EDS dynamic!); EDS endpoints (health!), outliers eject (panic thresholds!); `envoy --mode validate` checks — dynamic config (no restarts!), ejection tuned (flapping guarded!), validated (CI!)."),
    ("apache mpm security evasive", "MPM event (`MaxRequestWorkers` = RAM÷process!, `ThreadsPerChild`!) tuned; mod_security CRS (paranoia 1→4 staged!) + mod_evasive (DOSHashTableSize!) + mod_qos control; `mod_pagespeed` filters (lazy/combine!) — MPM sized (memory math!), CRS staged (false positives tuned!), evasive thresholds (legit bursts allowed!)."),
    ("varnish vcl grace saint", "VCL `vcl_recv` (pass/pipe/hash!) + `vcl_backend_response` (TTL/grace/keep!) + bans (`ban req.url ~`) purge + saintmode (sick backends!) — grace serves stale (origin down!), bans invalidate (patterns!), saintmode routes around sick (health!)."),
    ("tpm2 pcr seal unseal", "`tpm2_createprimary -C o` + `tpm2_create/createLoaded` + `tpm2_unseal` binds secrets to PCRs (measured boot!); PCR policy changes on update (re-seal planned!) — sealed to state (tampered ≠ unseal!), updates re-seal (scheduled!), recovery documented (bricked risk!)."),
    ("sssd cache enumerate debug", "SSSD (`enumerate = false` perf!, `cache_credentials = true` offline logins!, `sssctl cache-remove` flushes!) + `sssd -i -d 3` debugs; `getent passwd user@dom` verifies — enumerate off (large dirs!), cache on (offline!), debug leveled (logs sized!)."),
    ("ansible collections vault", "Collections (`ansible-galaxy collection install`, `requirements.yml` pinned versions!) + Vault (`ansible-vault encrypt_string`, vault IDs per env!) + dynamic inventory (constructed groups!) — collections pinned (breaking updates!), vault IDs separated (prod/dev!), inventories constructed (groups computed!)."),
    ("maas curtin commission hooks", "MAAS (`maas $P machines commission` hardware inventory + tests!; power drivers IPMI/Redfish verified!) + curtin `early/late-commands` (in-target!) + `curthooks` — commissioning data reviewed (firmware!), power tested (cycles!), hooks idempotent (re-runs safe!)."),
    ("kickstart anaconda text", "Kickstart (`%packages --excludedocs`, `%pre/%post --nochroot/--chroot`, `network --bootproto=static`, `rootpw --iscrypted`!) + `inst.text` unattended; `ksvalidator` lints — kickstarts linted (syntax!), passwords hashed (never plain!), logs preserved (`/root/anaconda-ks.cfg`!)."),
    ("cobbler snippets inheritance", "Cobbler distros/profiles/systems (inheritance chain!); snippets (`SNIPPET('...')` shared code!); `cobbler sync` regenerates (TFTP/dhcpd!) — snippets deduplicate (common code once!), inheritance layered (defaults→role→host!), sync verified (boot tested!)."),
    ("foreman katello content", "Foreman host groups (params inheritance!) + Smart Proxies (DHCP/DNS/TFTP per site!) + Katello lifecycle (Library→Dev→Stage→Prod!) + composite content views (atomic sets!) — groups model fleets (params!), proxies per site (latency!), lifecycles promote (tested!)."),
    ("insights compliance policies", "Insights advisor (rules: security/perf!), compliance policies (OpenSCAP profiles, scheduled scans!), vulnerability (CVE exposure!), remediations (Ansible auto-fix, scoped!) — registered (inventory!), remediations reviewed (auto-apply scoped!), compliance scheduled (drift caught!)."),
    ("leapp answerfile inhibitors", "Leapp `preupgrade` inhibitors listed (all green required!) + `/var/log/leapp/answerfile` pre-answered (unattended!) + actors custom — inhibitors resolved (zero outstanding!), answerfile complete (prompts kill!), snapshot first (rollback!)."),
    ("auditd immutable rules", "Rules (`-w /etc/shadow -p wa -k identity`, `-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -S execve`!) + `immutable` (`-e 2`, reboot to change!) + `audisp-remote` forwarding (central SIEM!) — rules versioned (git!), immutable prod (tamper-evident!), forwarded (local logs lie!)."),
