    ("cte recursive hierarchy", "`WITH RECURSIVE sub AS (SELECT ... WHERE id=1 UNION ALL SELECT e.* FROM emp e JOIN sub s ON e.mgr=s.id)` walks trees/graphs in SQL — org charts, BOMs, threads without application loops."),
    ("window frame rows", "`SUM(x) OVER (PARTITION BY d ORDER BY t ROWS BETWEEN 6 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW)` rolling windows; `RANGE` (value peers) vs `ROWS` (physical) vs `GROUPS` — frames define analytics, defaults mislead."),
